# Osteomancer Adept (CR 611.2a, 601.3): "Until end of turn, you may cast creature spells from your graveyard ..." is an effect of the
# resolved ability, not a static ability of the Adept, so it lasts the turn whatever becomes of the Adept, its finality rider too. Turn 1
# Bot1 casts the Adept, Mox Ruby and Faithless Looting (discarding Grizzly Bears and a Plains). On turn 3 the Adept taps, and once the
# ability has resolved Bot1 kills it with a Lightning Bolt. The Bears are still cast from the graveyard, foraging three of the other cards
# there, and enter with a finality counter.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Black Lotus
Osteomancer Adept
Faithless Looting
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Grizzly Bears
Plains
Plains x17

